  body: "# Contributory and non-contributory Retirement Pension categories\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe chapter
    distinguishes Category A and B contributory Retirement Pensions from Category C and D non-contributory Retirement
    Pensions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThese categories have different conditions and dated scope. Non-contributory
    does not mean unconditional eligibility. Category C historical and survivor provisions and Category D residence
    and age conditions remain distinct.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 75011, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 75012, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=4).\n\
    - [DMG 75013, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69d8f248eb7e7bc565170231/dmg-Ch-75.pdf#page=4).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch75` — PDF SHA-256 `655e7acb31f09f5169efbe40419091ee479f88c0c45b65c7a507b042b67712f9`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `0d037880d2aeaff1be89235ee987ca4acb1c839fcf1ead8b8be2daa9f6795465`.\n"
